<!--
  =========================================================================
  File        : colors.xml
  Project     : Smart Solar Microgrid Trading System - SE4040 Assignment 1
  Author      : NIMSARA R V P P (IT 23215306)
  Description : The brand colours, named by what they are for.

  A name like brand_green says what a colour is for. Changing the shade
  later is then one edit here, not a search for a hex code in every layout.

  ON CONTRAST
        The brand greens were checked against white before being used.

          Eco Green    #3A9D3F  3.46 : 1 on white
          Light Green  #6DBE45  2.31 : 1
          Energy Green #7BCB42  2.01 : 1

        WCAG asks for 4.5 : 1 for normal text. So none of those three may
        carry white button text or act as a link colour on a white page.
        They are fill and accent colours.

        brand_green_deep #2F7D33 was added for that job. It is the same
        hue and reaches 5.12 : 1, so buttons and links pass.

        On the navy surface the brighter greens are excellent, which is why
        dark mode uses Energy Green (7.30 : 1) as its primary.
  =========================================================================
-->
<resources>

    <!-- Brand -->
    <color name="brand_navy">#102A43</color>
    <color name="brand_navy_soft">#1B3A57</color>

    <!-- Interactive green. Passes on white, so buttons and links use it. -->
    <!--
      Nudged from #2F7D33 when the page behind it became tinted.

      On the old white page this green read 4.5 to 1 and passed. On the new
      #E9F0E9 page it dropped to 4.41, just under what WCAG asks for normal
      text, and it is used for normal text: the date under the node name on
      the QR screen sits straight on the page at 16sp.

      #2C7630 is the same green two shades down. 4.84 on the page, 5.61 on
      a white card, and 5.61 for white text on it as a button fill, so
      every place it is used now clears the bar.
    -->
    <color name="brand_green_deep">#2C7630</color>
    <color name="brand_green_deeper">#246A28</color>

    <!-- Fill and accent greens. Not for small text on white. -->
    <color name="brand_green">#3A9D3F</color>
    <color name="brand_green_light">#6DBE45</color>
    <color name="brand_green_energy">#7BCB42</color>
    <color name="brand_green_container">#DCEFDA</color>

    <!-- Neutrals -->
    <color name="ink">#102A43</color>
    <color name="ink_muted">#5A6B7C</color>
    <!--
      The page is tinted and the cards on it are white.

      It was the other way round: a white page with cards a shade off
      white. Measured, those two were 1.08 apart, which is not enough to
      see. While the cards still had a grey outline round them that did not
      matter, because the line drew the edge. The outline has gone, so the
      tone has to do the work on its own and the two had to separate.

      This way round measures 1.16, near the 1.28 the dark theme already
      had, and white cards on a tinted page is the plainer look of the two.

      Text was checked against the new page colour, not only against the
      cards: the body ink reads 13.0 to 1 on it and the muted ink 4.8 to 1,
      so both still clear the 4.5 that WCAG asks for.
    -->
    <color name="surface">#E9F0E9</color>
    <color name="surface_container">#FFFFFF</color>

    <!-- A step between the two, for a strip that is neither page nor card. -->
    <color name="surface_container_low">#F4F8F4</color>
    <color name="surface_container_high">#FFFFFF</color>
    <color name="hairline">#DDE5DC</color>

    <!-- Dark theme neutrals, tinted towards the brand navy -->
    <color name="ink_dark">#F4F8F4</color>
    <color name="ink_muted_dark">#9FB0C0</color>
    <color name="surface_dark">#0C1E30</color>
    <color name="surface_container_dark">#15324C</color>
    <color name="surface_container_low_dark">#112942</color>
    <color name="surface_container_high_dark">#1C4162</color>

    <!-- Status: reserved, never reused for decoration -->
    <color name="status_success">#2F7D33</color>
    <color name="status_warning">#B7791F</color>
    <color name="status_danger">#C53030</color>

    <color name="white">#FFFFFFFF</color>

</resources>
